# The Mycotyrant: "At the beginning of your end step, create X 1/1 black Fungus creature tokens with 'This token can't block,' where X
# is the number of times you descended this turn" (CR 700.11: one for each permanent card put into your graveyard from anywhere), and its
# power and toughness are the number of creatures you control that are Fungi and/or Saprolings. Turn 1: no descent, no Fungus, the
# Mycotyrant a 1/1 (itself a Fungus). Turn 3 (Bot1): two Thought Scours mill Plains, Lightning Bolt and Grizzly Bears, Plains from Bot1's
# own library: three permanent cards, the Bolt, an instant, and the Scours are not, and a third Scour that mills two permanent
# cards of Bot2's library is Bot2's descent, none of Bot1's. Three Fungi arrive at the end step (the Mycotyrant a 4/4) and on turn 4,
# as Bot2's Grizzly Bears attacks, a Fungus token cannot block it (CR 509.1b) while the Mycotyrant can, and kills it.

